# GitHub delivery lifecycle

For issue, code, config, CI, security, or rule work, load `.cursor/skills/github-delivery/SKILL.md`.

These session gates are **MUST**. They override casual user phrasing ("quick fix", "just tweak"). Only an **explicit** user override ("stay on this branch", "leave as draft", "commit locally only") can waive them -- and that waiver MUST be stated in the PR body if work ships.

## Required

1. Inspect the issue body, labels, owner, project, milestone, relationships, and Development links before work.
2. Code/config/CI/rule changes use a feature branch and a ready PR. Direct `master` push is only for status-only work or explicit user instruction.
3. Every actionable issue has kind, priority (labels `P0`..`P3` only -- do not invent a second Priority project field), domain, concrete acceptance/Next, human owner while active, and a [Nova Delivery](https://github.com/users/aaltaay/projects/1) project item. Canonical board (do not recreate): user project number `1`, owner `aaltaay`, id `PVT_kwHOAXJK5M4Ab7Vq`, Status options Todo / In Progress / Done. When the token allows, run `gh project item-add 1 --owner aaltaay --url <issue-or-pr html_url>` and default Status to **Todo** unless it is already In Progress. Classic `GITHUB_TOKEN` and the Cloud Agent GitHub App typically lack `project` scope (`403` or `Could not resolve to a ProjectV2`); owner `gh` as `aaltaay` can mutate, and Actions uses repo secret `NOVA_PROJECT_TOKEN`. On 403, report that limitation -- never claim the item exists, never create a new project.
4. Milestones and relationships are conditional facts, never filler.
5. Use `Closes #NNN` only when the whole issue is complete. Partial work uses `Refs #NNN`, gets an evidence comment, and leaves the issue open.
6. Verification is advisory. Run relevant checks for feedback, but do not wait for tests, builds, browser checks or Desktop pack before merging. Report pending/failed results truthfully.
7. After closing a deferred issue, run `py -3 tools/deferred_log.py refresh-index` and ship the refreshed index.
8. After a PR is merged or closed, **delete the head branch in the same session** if it is still on origin. GitHub `delete_branch_on_merge` is on (backup sweep). Do not skip the check. Run `git fetch origin --prune`, then `py -3 tools/stale_pr_branches.py`. If the head is still listed, run `py -3 tools/pr_delivery.py delete-closed --ref <branch>` (or the GitHub "Delete branch" control) and prune again. Never delete `master` / `main`, and never delete a branch that still has an **open** PR.
9. **Master branch protection** is required: no force-push, no deletion, admins included, with no required status checks. Do not require reviews (solo deadlock). Do not require a PR to push (status-only master commits). The AI news digest must not push master -- it opens a ready PR from `chore/ai-news-digest`. Check with `py -3 tools/master_branch_protection.py check`. `apply` needs Administration (Cloud Agent GitHub App is 403). `check` can still pass from the public branch `protection` summary. Public Nova unlocks the setting on GitHub Free. A private personal repo still needs GitHub Pro.
10. **GitHub Actions merges ready PRs.** Opening a verified non-draft PR is the agent finish line. Do not wait for the human to say merge. `tools/pr_delivery.py` plus `.github/workflows/pr-delivery.yml` and the CI `Auto-merge` job merge without waiting for CI, then delete the head. A ready PR merges no sooner than five minutes after it opens, and not while an automated review is still running on its head, so review findings land on the open branch rather than on `master` (`pr-delivery-timing.mdc`); findings themselves never block. Draft or label `do-not-merge` is the only hold, and only under item 12. Conflicts hold PRs; failed checks do not.
11. **Clean start and mandatory finish** are `AGENTS.md` §5.1, the one home (ADR 051): a new focused branch from `origin/master` on a clean tree; verify, commit, push, a **ready (non-draft)** PR from `.github/pull_request_template.md` as the finish line. Draft or `do-not-merge` only on an explicit user hold or a documented hard external blocker, never because CI is still running.

## Closure after merge

A merged PR or a `Closes` line is not evidence that the issue closed: read each named issue's actual state after the merge, and close only completed work through an authorized issue-write path. The mechanics (`issues: write` on every merging job, the parser's exclusions, the readback after a refused write) are `tools/pr_delivery_actions.py`, pinned by `tools/test_pr_delivery.py` and `tools/test_pr_delivery_workflow.py`.

If GitHub plan or token permissions prevent Projects or branch protection, report the exact limitation; never claim the metadata or protection exists. Public source home is `aaltaay/Nova`; `aaltaay/Nova-public` is a private archive.

Current-tip preservation overrides mandatory head deletion: `branch-cleanup.mdc`. Owner policy (2026-09-20): all verification is advisory; ready PRs merge while checks run or fail; no required status checks; force-push and deletion protection stay.
